      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`test_dsa_glm52_hisparse.py::_test_long_context_spec_swap` fails intermittently, in both greedy and non-greedy runs. The model retrieves the correct code, but the test sends `ignore_eos`, and stripping special tokens removes the EOS between the answer and whatever is generated after it. When that later text starts with a digit, the `(?!\\d)` boundary check fails:\n\n- CI (temperature 0): `7393911. What is the name of the language...`\n- Local (temperature 0.6): `739391555023\\n555023...`\n\n## Modifications\n\nPass `skip_special_tokens: False` so the EOS token stays in the returned text (e.g. `739391<|user|>1. What...`). All GLM-5.2 stop tokens (`<|endoftext|>`, `<|user|>`, `<|observation|>`) are special tokens in the tokenizer. The check is just as strict as before: a wrong code, or extra digits with no EOS in between, still fails.\n\n## Testing\n\nChecked the decoded output against the `nvidia/GLM-5.2-NVFP4` tokenizer. The full 8xB200 test has not been rerun yet.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #38998620292](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38998620292)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38998620232](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38998620232)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #38998620305](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38998620305)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
